oliver: Quick check — I'm proposing we add an explicit `event_type` field to streaming deltas to make mid-stream function/tool-call payloads unambiguous. Right now clients infer from `delta` + `done` which is brittle for func args that interleave with normal text. I'd like sync on compatibility approach before I land a runtime change.

amanda: pinged on the PR, can you paste a minimal example of old vs proposed payload?

oliver: current (simplified):
```json
{ "type": "delta", "role": "assistant", "content": "{\"name\": \"search\", \"args\": \"{\"q\":\"redwood\"}\"}" }
{ "type": "delta", "role": "assistant", "content": "more args..." }
{ "type": "done" }
```
proposed: add `event_type` + `sequence_id`:
```json
{ "type": "delta", "event_type": "func_start", "sequence_id": 1, "func": "search" }
{ "type": "delta", "event_type": "func_body", "sequence_id": 2, "content": "{\"q\":\"redwood\"}" }
{ "type": "delta", "event_type": "func_end", "sequence_id": 3 }
{ "type": "delta", "event_type": "final", "sequence_id": 4 }
```
This makes assembly deterministic and explicit.

kai: I like `event_type`. Two compatibility notes: 1) don't break clients that only look for `done`/`delta` — keep emitting `done` boolean or an equivalent for transition period. 2) SDKs need a clear migration path. Suggest add `legacy_done: true` for a window.

sara: ordering question — some clients assemble tokens and don't expect separate `func_body` chunks. If we add `sequence_id` that's helpful. Also we should define whether `sequence_id` is per-message or global per-stream. I vote per-message (monotonic within one top-level response).

oliver: agreed: `sequence_id` per response (reset per response_id). Also propose possible values for `event_type`: `chunk` | `func_start` | `func_body` | `func_end` | `final`. Example for a func that returns streaming partial JSON:
```json
{ "response_id": "r_123", "event_type": "func_start", "sequence_id": 1, "func": "summarize" }
{ "response_id": "r_123", "event_type": "func_body", "sequence_id": 2, "content": "{\"part\":1}" }
{ "response_id": "r_123", "event_type": "func_body", "sequence_id": 3, "content": "{\"part\":2}" }
{ "response_id": "r_123", "event_type": "func_end", "sequence_id": 4 }
{ "response_id": "r_123", "event_type": "final", "sequence_id": 5 }
```

amanda: OK. Who's going to update the JS + Python SDKs to consume `event_type` and `sequence_id`? We should also draft a deprecation plan for the old implicit behavior.

kai: i'll take SDK changes (js) — will add assembly helpers that accept the new stream and fallback to legacy parsing if `event_type` absent. Sara can you own py?

sara: I can do the py SDK changes. Also we need unit tests that validate assembly for mixed streams (legacy + event_type).

sara: small question — how do we handle model fallback mid-stream (model A starts func, model B finishes?) we might need `fallback_reason` or an `inconsistent_stream` event.

oliver: good catch. propose `func_end` can include optional `fallback_to` and `fallback_reason`. If a different model finishes the call we emit `func_end { "fallback_to": "model-b", "fallback_reason": "capacity" }`. Clients can surface that in logs and optionally retry.

amanda: seems reasonable. For deprecation timeline I'm thinking 8 weeks after server flags are enabled and SDKs released. Anyone object?

kai: 8 weeks OK. Also add a feature flag so customers can opt-in earlier for dedicated/private.

sara: add integration test vectors in `eng-runtime` repo and a small harness that asserts reassembly equals expected string. I can add that to the py changes.

oliver: quick runtime implementation note — we'll emit both forms during rollout: keep `type: done` for compatibility and add `event_type`. Servers should set `legacy_done=true` for the window. I'll open PR to runtime and eng-runtime with tests.

ci-bot: deploy/infra: gating build for `runtime/streaming-event-type` passed on linux-x64. :white_check_mark:

amanda: I'll draft the RFC + docs page for the API contract and link the SDK PRs. After docs + tests + SDKs are green we can flip the opt-in flag and start deprecation notices.

kai: I'll put the JS assembly helper behind a feature flag and include migration notes in changelog.

sara: sounds good. Can we list the exact schema fields for the docs? I'll copy from this thread and format.

oliver: will do — thanks all. I'll open the runtime PRs now and tag @amanda @kai @sara for reviews. :thumbsup:
